# Create the `room-clr` Spring Boot project

Run the following commands in PowerShell to download the project from Spring Initializr and extract it into the `room-clr` folder:

```powershell
Set-Location "D:\AI DEV\SpringBoot 3 tutorial"

curl.exe --fail --location --silent --show-error --retry 3 -G "https://start.spring.io/starter.zip" `
  --data-urlencode "type=maven-project" `
  --data-urlencode "language=java" `
  --data-urlencode "javaVersion=21" `
  --data-urlencode "packaging=jar" `
  --data-urlencode "groupId=com.soulemane.lil" `
  --data-urlencode "artifactId=room-clr" `
  --data-urlencode "packageName=com.soulemane.lil.room.clr" `
  -o ".\room-clr.zip"

if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "Project download failed; check the error above." }

Expand-Archive -Path ".\room-clr.zip" -DestinationPath ".\room-clr"
```

## Run the application

Run Spring Boot through the Maven wrapper from the project folder. Do not compile
`RoomClrApplication.java` directly with `javac`; that command does not include
the Spring Boot dependencies.

```powershell
Set-Location "D:\AI DEV\SpringBoot 3 tutorial\room-clr"
.\mvnw.cmd spring-boot:run
```